course: dictionary
lesson: 2805
title: Slang and respect
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Diss is slang, a casual word people use with friends, in music and online. It is not usually a word for school reports. In «Don't diss my football team», diss means "don't be rude about my football team". Diss is short for disrespect, and you already know dis- means not or the opposite.
explain: To diss someone is to show them disrespect by insulting them or saying unkind things about them. Diss can also be a noun, an insult, especially in a rap song, which is called a diss track. The clue is how the other person feels: they are hurt, and the speaker is not being kind.
explain: Knowing this word helps you spot when someone is being mean, even online. Ask yourself: is this comment kind, or is it meant to hurt? If it is a diss, you do not have to join in. You can choose words that show respect instead.
fact: Diss is slang, so it is informal and is mostly used among friends or in music.
fact: «Diss» is short for «disrespect»; dis- means not or the opposite.
fact: Diss comes from hip hop slang in the USA in the 1980s.
fact: «Diss» can be a verb (to diss someone, disses, dissed, dissing) or a noun (a diss, disses).
fact: A «diss track» is a rap song that insults someone.
exercise: «Don't diss my football team.» What does diss mean here? | To join their team | To ask them a question | *To be rude about someone or something | To cheer loudly for them
exercise: In a rap song, a «diss» is what? | A kind present for a friend | *An insult aimed at someone | A quiet part of the song | A type of dance move
exercise: Diss is short for which longer word? | dish | *disrespect | distance | discover
test: Which sentence shows respect rather than dissing someone? | Your team is useless, go home | Everyone laughs at your rubbish team | *Well played to your team today, good effort | You always lose, so stop trying
test: Why is dissing someone a form of being mean online? | Because it is a long word | Because it is only used in old books | *Because it insults people and says unkind things about them | Because it makes people laugh and feel happy
exam: What is the kindest thing to do when someone starts to diss your friend? | Post a diss back online | Walk away and never speak to anyone again | Join in and laugh | *Stand up for your friend and say that it is unkind
